        ;; with regard to the exact error value for truncated input.
        (set! (.-err dec) io/ErrUnexpectedEOF))

      (return (.-err dec)))

    (set! (.-hadPeeked dec) false)
    (set! (.-hadEOF dec) false)
    (jsonv2/Unmarshal b v (.-opts dec))))
















^{:go/end 109} (go/method Buffered "Buffered returns a reader of the data remaining in the unread buffer,\nwhich may contain zero or more bytes.\nThis is the data already consumed from the input [io.Reader],\nbut not yet read by a [Decoder.Decode] or [Decoder.Token] call.\nIt may contain bytes that do not form valid JSON as it has not yet\nbeen validated according to the JSON grammar.\nThe exact amount of buffered data is an implementation detail\nof the Decoder and may change over time.\n\nIt is the caller's responsibility to concatenate this buffer with\nthe remainder of the input Reader to obtain the full sequence\nof bytes after the last decoded JSON value.\n\nThe reader is valid until the next call to [Decoder.Decode] or [Decoder.Token].\n" ^io/Reader [^{:tag (* Decoder)} dec]
  (bytes/NewReader (.UnreadBuffer (.-dec dec))))



